**Finding 5 (Medium): extract a shared predicate instead of 28 inline copies.**

`core/schemas/secretvar.go:455` already exports `ShouldPreserveStored()` with exactly this intent, used by `handlers/config.go`, `handlers/plugins.go`, and `lib/config.go`. It differs from this inline predicate only on empty values (it preserves; your empty-value subtest requires pass-through so validation fires), so reusing it verbatim would be wrong here - but that is an argument for a named sibling, not for 28 hand-inlined copies:

```go
// core/schemas/secretvar.go
// IsMaskedPlaceholder reports whether the value is a client-side redaction
// placeholder (not a secret ref) that must never overwrite a stored credential.
func (e *SecretVar) IsMaskedPlaceholder() bool {
    return e != nil && e.IsRedacted() && !e.IsFromSecret()
}
```

One tested helper also covers the ~15 individual guards the new test does not exercise, and gives the follow-up fixes in `providers.go:486-502` and `mcp.go:1086,1652` (which still carry the old `Equals`-gated bug) the same single source of truth. When the redaction shapes change next (e.g. a new sentinel), only one place needs updating.

Also a tradeoff worth a log line: any redacted-shaped intentional input (literal `[REDACTED]`, all-asterisk string) is now silently dropped with a 200; a warning log when the guard fires would make that observable.

